# @rt-category Test Scenes
# @rt-description A translucent plate lit by a point light behind it, seen from the front. Checks light passing through a diffuse-transmission surface.
# @rt-performance Fast
# @rt-size 40
# diffuse-transmission-point-light.pbrt -- a diffuse-transmission plate lit by one point light behind it, seen from the front, and (second half of the
# test) with the light in front. The answer is a closed form at the centre of the plate.
#
# A point light cannot be hit by a BSDF-sampled bounce, so it is only ever seen through next-event estimation. The GPU backends gave a diffuse-transmission
# surface no light sampling at all (a BSDF-only estimator that is unbiased for area lights but cannot see a point, spot or distant light), so the plate was
# black under any such light. pbrt-v4's DiffuseTransmissionBxDF is R/pi on the side of the light that wo is on and T/pi through the surface.
#
# Plate R = 0.3, T = 0.5, z = 0, 40 x 40 (so every direction a pixel sees is within the plate). Camera at z = +6 looking at the centre with a 2 degree
# field of view: every pixel sees the centre of the plate at normal incidence, wo = +z.
#   light BEHIND (z = -3, intensity 90): E = 90 / 9 = 10 at the plate, transmitted radiance T/pi * E = 0.5 / pi * 10 = 1.5915
#   light IN FRONT (z = +3, intensity 90): E = 10, reflected radiance R/pi * E = 0.3 / pi * 10 = 0.9549
# The light is placed by the "Translate" below; the test renders both scenes (this file is the "behind" one, the "-front" file the other).
#
# Original, not derived from any distributed scene, so it carries no licence constraints.

LookAt  0 0 6    0 0 0    0 1 0
Camera "perspective" "float fov" [ 2 ]

Film "rgb" "integer xresolution" [ 16 ] "integer yresolution" [ 16 ]
Sampler "halton" "integer pixelsamples" [ 64 ]

WorldBegin

AttributeBegin
  Translate 0 0 -3
  LightSource "point" "rgb I" [ 90 90 90 ]
AttributeEnd

Material "diffusetransmission" "rgb reflectance" [ 0.3 0.3 0.3 ] "rgb transmittance" [ 0.5 0.5 0.5 ]
Shape "trianglemesh" "integer indices" [ 0 1 2  0 2 3 ]
  "point3 P" [ -20 -20 0   20 -20 0   20 20 0   -20 20 0 ]
